# Keep the build context small and, more importantly, keep secrets and local
# state out of the image entirely.
#
# `.env` is the one that matters: it holds the live SMTP password, the SMS API
# key and JWT_SECRET. A COPY that pulled it in would bake production
# credentials into every layer of a published image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

node_modules
dist
.git
.github
*.log
coverage

# Tests are not shipped. They are run in CI against the source, and the build
# stage excludes them from `dist` anyway (see tsconfig.build.json).
test

README.md
